  ["kotoba-lang/num gains N-D tensors, broadcasting, reshape, axis reductions (Phase 1),
    and a real live GPU backend (Phase 2: Deno + native WebGPU (navigator.gpu) -> wgpu ->
    Metal, promoting the already-verified verify/metal_contract.js pattern into num's own
    IBackend/IGpuDevice, not just a standalone test)"
   "new safetensors reader, pure .cljc (Phase 3), loading real HuggingFace-published
    TRELLIS/Hunyuan3D-2/UniRig checkpoint format (JSON header + raw tensor bytes, no
    pickle) into Phase-1 N-D tensors"
   "kotoba-lang/torch gains its first real execution engine (Phase 3.5): an IBackend wired
    to num, so torch.core/run stops throwing 'shape-only' and actually computes"
   "attention (Phase 4), conv3d (Phase 5), sparse convolution + forward-only rasterization
    (Phase 6, hardest/most novel) are DESIGNED here but explicitly NOT implemented in this
    pass — do not treat this ADR as claiming TRELLIS/Hunyuan3D-2/UniRig can run yet"
   "motivated by evaluating the real, already-existing 11-node Mac mini M4 16GB fleet
    (kotoba-lang/murakumo/fleet.edn) as an alternative to the unbuilt cloud H100/A100 fleet
    (ADR-2607031600) for kami-gen-ml3d (ADR-2607051120) / :autorig (ADR-0048 §2)"]
